import{_ as t,o as a,c as o,a3 as n}from"./chunks/framework.Ce1AN3zV.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"The admin area","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"docs/admin.md","filePath":"docs/admin.md"}'),s={name:"docs/admin.md"};function i(r,e,d,c,h,l){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="the-admin-area" tabindex="-1">The admin area <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-admin-area" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The admin area&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The admin area is where the maintainer looks after the catalog, the accounts and the server&#39;s settings. It is a section of the website under <code>/admin</code>, backed by routes under <code>/api/v1/admin/</code>. The work is tracked in <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/26" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#26</a>.</p><h2 id="who-can-open-it" tabindex="-1">Who can open it <a class="header-anchor" href="#who-can-open-it" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Who can open it&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Admin is a role on the account</strong> (<code>member</code> or <code>admin</code>), not a scope anyone can ask for (<a href="./adr/0020-every-credential-resolves-to-one-caller">ADR 0020</a>).</li><li><strong>Only the website&#39;s sign-in reaches it.</strong> An admin route answers 401 to an anonymous caller and 403 to anyone who is not an admin signed in through the website: a member, an admin on the phone app, a personal access token or a third-party app.</li><li><strong>The website signs in with cookies</strong> (<code>POST /api/v1/web/session</code>, see <a href="./the-api">the API</a>). The server reads the access cookie only for the website client, and a write whose <code>Origin</code> is not the website&#39;s gets 403, which is the CSRF defence of <a href="./adr/0020-every-credential-resolves-to-one-caller">ADR 0020</a>. The API answers the website&#39;s origin with <code>Access-Control-Allow-Credentials</code>, so the page calls it with <code>credentials: &#39;include&#39;</code>.</li><li><strong>One admin for now.</strong> There are no finer rights.</li></ul><h2 id="the-screens" tabindex="-1">The screens <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-screens" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The screens&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The admin lives at <code>/admin</code> on the website (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-shell.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mockups</a>). With no admin session it shows the sign-in; the page asks <code>GET /api/v1/me</code>, and a member who signs in is signed out again at once with the same &quot;wrong email or password&quot; message, so the screen never says who is an admin. Once signed in it shows the <code>CpDrawer</code> shell, with the audit log, the accounts, the settings and the status. The sidebar lists only the screens that exist; each admin feature adds its own entry. A <strong>Coach Poulpy app</strong> link at the bottom of the sidebar goes back to <a href="./web-app">the web app</a>.</p><h2 id="accounts" tabindex="-1">Accounts <a class="header-anchor" href="#accounts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Accounts&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Accounts</strong> screen is a paged table of every account (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-accounts.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mockups</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-accounts-details.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">details</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-accounts-filtered.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">filtered</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-accounts-none.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">no match</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-accounts-delete.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">delete</a>). Each row shows the email, role, whether the email is confirmed, whether sign-in is blocked and the creation date. Every column sorts (a click flips the direction); the email filter matches part of the address and the role, email status and sign-in filters narrow the list. Eight accounts show per page, with <code>CpPagination</code> and the count below. Picking a row opens its details in the <code>CpSidePanel</code>, floating over the page from the right with a dim backdrop (the table never moves; a click outside or Escape closes it). The state is in the address (<code>/admin/accounts?q=…&amp;role=…&amp;sort=…&amp;order=…&amp;page=…&amp;account=&lt;id&gt;</code>), so a view can be bookmarked and the back button steps through it (<a href="./web-app#navigation-lives-in-the-url">Navigation lives in the URL</a>); the audit log is <code>/admin</code>. Nothing here shows a workout or health data. The panel holds three actions, each written to the audit log with the account&#39;s id as the target (never its address):</p><ul><li><strong>Disable</strong> blocks sign-in and signs every device of the account out, access and refresh tokens included. It is reversible: <strong>Enable</strong> lets the account sign in again. A disabled account is refused at sign-in with the same &quot;wrong email or password&quot; answer as any other refusal.</li><li><strong>Delete</strong> removes the account and every row of it through the same code as the user&#39;s own deletion, once the admin has typed the account&#39;s email again.</li><li>An admin can&#39;t disable or delete their own account (<code>409 own-account</code>).</li></ul><p>Filtering, sorting and paging happen on the server (<code>AdminAccounts.list</code>, which reads every account row and cuts the page in memory, enough for a back office; move it into SQL if accounts reach the hundreds of thousands). The routes are <code>GET /api/v1/admin/accounts/{id}</code> for one account (a link opens an account that isn&#39;t on the page), <code>GET /api/v1/admin/accounts</code> with <code>q</code>, <code>role</code>, <code>confirmed</code> (<code>yes</code>/<code>no</code>), <code>signIn</code> (<code>active</code>/<code>disabled</code>), <code>sort</code> (<code>email</code>, <code>role</code>, <code>confirmed</code>, <code>signIn</code>, <code>created</code>), <code>order</code>, <code>page</code> and <code>size</code>, answering <code>{accounts, total}</code> (a word that isn&#39;t allowed is a <code>400 bad-query</code>), <code>POST /api/v1/admin/accounts/{id}/disable</code>, <code>POST /api/v1/admin/accounts/{id}/enable</code> and <code>DELETE /api/v1/admin/accounts/{id}</code> with <code>{&quot;confirmEmail&quot;: …}</code>, all described in the OpenAPI document and all for an admin signed in through the website.</p><h2 id="settings" tabindex="-1">Settings <a class="header-anchor" href="#settings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Settings&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Settings</strong> screen at <code>/admin/settings</code> changes the server without a deploy (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-settings-mail.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mockups</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-settings-mail-invalid.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">invalid address</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-settings-mail-test-ok.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">test sent</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-settings-mail-test-failed.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">test failed</a>). Its one setting so far is the <strong>from-address</strong> of the emails.</p><ul><li><strong>Only non-secret settings live in the database</strong>, one row per setting in the <code>settings</code> table (<code>ServerSettings</code>). The SMTP host, port, user and password stay in the environment (<a href="./deploying-the-server">Deploying the server</a>) and are not shown or editable here.</li><li><strong><code>MAIL_FROM</code> is the default until a from-address is saved.</strong> A saved one applies to the next email, with no restart: every email goes through <code>SettingsMailer</code>, which reads the setting when it sends. An address alone (<code>hello@example.com</code>) or with a name (<code>Coach Poulpy &lt;hello@example.com&gt;</code>) is accepted; anything else is refused (<code>400 invalid-address</code>) and nothing is saved.</li><li><strong>Saving writes <code>admin.settings.mail-from</code> to the audit log</strong>, with the masked address (<code>h***@example.com</code>) as the target.</li><li><strong>Send test email</strong> sends a message to the signed-in admin&#39;s own address with the saved settings and shows whether the mail server took it or, in crimson with an icon, what it answered (<code>535 Authentication failed</code>).</li><li><strong>The last send is remembered.</strong> <code>SettingsMailer.last</code> keeps when the last email (a test or any other) went, which kind it was, to whom (masked) and the mail server&#39;s error if any, for the <a href="#status">Status</a> screen. It lives in memory, so a restart forgets it.</li></ul><p>The routes are <code>GET /api/v1/admin/settings</code> (<code>{mailFrom, mailFromSaved}</code>), <code>POST /api/v1/admin/settings/mail-from</code> with <code>{&quot;mailFrom&quot;: …}</code> and <code>POST /api/v1/admin/settings/test-email</code> (<code>{sent, error}</code>), for an admin signed in through the website. The screen keeps no state of its own beyond its path.</p><h2 id="status" tabindex="-1">Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#status" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Status&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Status</strong> screen at <code>/admin/status</code> says what the server can do right now (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-status.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mockups</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-status-mail-missing.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mail not configured</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/admin-status-mail-failed.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">last send failed</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/340" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#340</a>). It only reads: nothing on it changes the server or sends an email. It starts with mail and can take other checks later, each its own card.</p><ul><li><strong>Mail</strong> says whether a mail server is configured, which is whether <code>SMTP_HOST</code> is set. Without it the server has no fallback: every email fails with <code>No mail server is set: SMTP_HOST is unset</code>, nothing of it is printed to the log, and the card shows <strong>Not configured</strong> with the reason, in crimson with an icon. With it, the card says how the last email since the start went: sent, when and which kind (confirmation, password reset or test), or the mail server&#39;s error in crimson. The SMTP host, user and password are never shown.</li><li><strong>Pending registrations</strong> lists the accounts whose email isn&#39;t confirmed yet, newest first (the last 100): the address, when it signed up and when its latest confirmation link expires. Signing up again sends a new link, so the date moves. No email is sent from here and there is no action on a row; on a laptop with no mail server, this is where a developer sees who signed up, and confirms them in Postgres (<a href="./the-api#trying-it-locally">Trying it locally</a>).</li></ul><p>The routes are <code>GET /api/v1/admin/status</code> (<code>{mail: {configured, lastSend: {at, kind, sent, error} | null}}</code>) and <code>GET /api/v1/admin/pending-registrations</code> (<code>{registrations: [{email, signedUpAt, linkExpiresAt}]}</code>), for an admin signed in through the website.</p><p>The public side is the web app&#39;s <code>/status</code> page (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/app-status.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mockups</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/blob/main/design/mockups/agreed/web/app-status-down.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">down</a>), which anyone can open. It asks <code>GET /api/v1/status</code> and shows only whether Coach Poulpy is up or down, down too when the server can&#39;t be reached; it never says how the server is configured, and a test holds it to that.</p><h2 id="making-the-first-admin" tabindex="-1">Making the first admin <a class="header-anchor" href="#making-the-first-admin" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Making the first admin&quot;">​</a></h2><p>No endpoint makes an admin. Set <code>ADMIN_EMAIL</code> in the <code>production</code> environment (<a href="./releasing#deploy-the-server">Releasing</a>) and deploy: when the server starts, the confirmed account with that address becomes an admin. An address with no confirmed account does nothing, so signing up first with someone else&#39;s address cannot take the role. The promotion is written to the audit log.</p><h2 id="the-audit-log" tabindex="-1">The audit log <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-audit-log" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The audit log&quot;">​</a></h2><p>An admin action is an <code>AdminAction</code> event (who, what, the target), sent through http4k&#39;s <code>Events</code> like any other event. One sink stores it in the <code>admin_audit</code> table (who is empty when the server itself did it, as at start-up; rows stay when the admin&#39;s own account is deleted), and another prints it to the server log, which the log shipping picks up. <code>GET /api/v1/admin/audit</code> returns the last 100 rows, and the first screen of the admin shows them. Each admin feature emits an <code>AdminAction</code> for its writes; tests check it with <code>RecordingEvents</code>.</p><p>Sensitive values are values4k types that print masked: <code>EmailAddress</code> prints as <code>a***@example.com</code>, so an address that reaches a log or an event by accident stays hidden, and the real one is read with <code>.value</code> only where it is needed. An event never carries a password or an unmasked address.</p><h2 id="what-comes-next" tabindex="-1">What comes next <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-comes-next" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What comes next&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The catalog (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/337" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#337</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/338" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#338</a>). The status will take more checks, such as the database and the catalog version, and log viewing is its own issue.</p>',26)])])}const p=t(s,[["render",i]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
